### Testing

- Mock the registry a function reads or writes, as you would the filesystem or network; never touch the real one from a unit test.
- Test parameter validation and the `ShouldProcess` branch explicitly; `-WhatIf` must produce no side effect.
<!-- Project-specific / PowerShell-Testing -->

### Common Mistakes

- Alias in a script: an alias (`gci`, `%`, `?`, `echo`) left in a script => write the full cmdlet name.
- Text instead of objects: a function emitting formatted text that a caller must regex-parse back into data => return objects.
- String-built command: `Invoke-Expression` running a command built by string concatenation => use a script block or splatted parameters.
- Missing `ShouldProcess`: a state-changing function without `SupportsShouldProcess`, so `-WhatIf` and `-Confirm` silently do nothing => add it and gate the change with `$PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess(...)`.
- Unapproved verb: a verb outside the approved list (`Create-`, `Delete-`, `Update-`) forcing an import warning => pick the matching approved verb from `Get-Verb`.
- Global as parameter: a `$global:` variable standing in for a parameter or a module-scoped value => pass a parameter, or use a module-scoped variable.
<!-- Project-specific / PowerShell-Common Mistakes -->
